# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for MiNiFi C++ test runs.
#
# Wired in via TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=... in cmake/BuildTests.cmake.
# Format reference: https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/ThreadSanitizerSuppressions
#
# --- civetweb (vendored HTTP library) ---
# Shutdown-time races between mg_stop()/CivetServer::close() on the main thread
# and civetweb worker/master threads still draining connections, fully inside the
# civetweb library.
race:*civetweb-src*

# --- open62541 (vendored OPC UA library) ---
# Races in the server timer (batchTimerEntry/UA_Timer_add) and ua_server during
# OPC UA test server start/stop, plus open62541's own internal server-lock
# ordering (UA_LOCK/lockServer acquired in different orders on startup vs. the
# timer thread). Both stacks are entirely inside open62541.
race:*open62541*
deadlock:*open62541*

# --- Catch2 test framework (src/catch2) ---
# Fast-path assertion counters (assertionPassedFastPath/handleExpr) race when
# assertions are evaluated from multiple threads within a test.
race:*catch_run_context*

# --- BackTrace stack-dump signal handler (core-framework/src/utils/BackTrace.cpp) ---
# The SIGUSR2 handler that captures per-thread stack traces for the jstack/BackTrace
# diagnostic feature deliberately does non-async-signal-safe work (it allocates and
# takes a lock inside pull_trace()/handler()). This covers both "signal-unsafe call
# inside of a signal handler" and "signal handler spoils errno". Accepted as a
# diagnostic-only risk rather than reworked here.
signal:*BackTrace.cpp*
